َى اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، وَمَنْ أَخَذَ يُرِيدُ إِتْلاَفَهَا أَتْلَفَهُ اللَّهُ ‏\"‏‏.‏\nL70: Reference  |  : 【15†Sahih al-Bukhari 2387】\nL71: In-book reference  |  : Book 43, Hadith 3\nL72: USC-MSA web (English) reference  |  : Vol. 3, Book 41, Hadith 572\nL73:   (deprecated numbering scheme)\nL74: \nL75: Report Error | Share | Copy ▼\nL76: \nL77: 【16†2386】【17†2388】\nL78: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih Muslim 102 - The Book of Faith - كتاب الإيمان - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/muslim%3A102)\nciteturn26view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/muslim:102\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/muslim:102; Total lines: 73\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: Quotes e.g. \"pledge allegiance\"\nL26: Searches for the whole phrase instead of individual words\nL27: \nL28: Wildcards e.g. test*\nL29: Matches any set of one or more characters. For example test* would result in test, tester, testers, etc.\nL30: \nL31: Fuzzy Search e.g. swore~\nL32: Finds terms that are similar in spelling. For example swore~ would result in swore, snore, score, etc.\nL33: Term Boosting e.g. pledge^4 hijrah\nL34: Boosts words with higher relevance. Here, the word pledge will have higher weight than hijrah\nL35: \nL36: Boolean Operators e.g. (\"pledge allegiance\" OR \"shelter) AND prayer\nL37: Create complex phrase and word queries by using Boolean logic.\nL38: \nL39: 【7†More ...】\nL40: \nL41: 【2†Home】 » 【8†Sahih Muslim】 » 【9†The Book of Faith - كتاب الإيمان】 » Hadith 102\nL42: \nL43: كتاب الإيمان\nL44: \nL45: 1\nL46: \nL47: The Book of Faith\nL48: \nL49: (43)\nL50: \nL51: Chapter: The Saying of the prophet (saws): \"Whoever deceives us is not one of us.\"\nL52: \nL53: (43)\nL54: باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ - صلى الله تعالى عليه وسلم - ‏\"‏ مَنْ غَشَّنَا فَلَيْسَ مِنَّا ‏\"‏\nL55: \nL56: Sahih Muslim 102\nL57: \nL58: It is narrated on the authority of Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) happened to pass by a heap of eatables (corn). He thrust his hand in that (heap) and his fingers were moistened. He said to the owner of that heap of eatables (corn):\nL59: What is this? He replied: Messenger of Allah, these have been drenched by rainfall. He (the Holy Prophet) remarked: Why did you not place this (the drenched part of the heap) over other eatables so that the people could see it? He who deceives is not of me (is not my follower).\nL60: وَحَدَّثَنِي 【10†يَحْيَى بْنُ أَيُّوبَ】، 【11†وَقُتَيْبَةُ】، 【12†وَابْنُ، حُجْرٍ】 جَمِيعًا عَنْ 【13†إِسْمَاعِيلَ بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ】، - قَالَ ابْنُ أَيُّوبَ حَدَّثَنَا إِسْمَاعِيلُ، - قَالَ أَخْبَرَنِي 【14†الْعَلاَءُ】، عَنْ 【15†أَبِيهِ】، عَنْ 【16†أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ】، ‏.‏ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم مَرَّ عَلَى صُبْرَةِ طَعَامٍ فَأَدْخَلَ يَدَهُ فِيهَا فَنَالَتْ أَصَابِعُهُ بَلَلاً فَقَالَ ‏\"‏ مَا هَذَا يَا صَاحِبَ الطَّعَامِ ‏\"‏ ‏.‏ قَالَ أَصَابَتْهُ السَّمَاءُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ‏.‏ قَالَ ‏\"‏ أَفَلاَ جَعَلْتَهُ فَوْقَ الطَّعَامِ كَىْ يَرَاهُ النَّاسُ مَنْ غَشَّ فَلَيْسَ مِنِّي ‏\"‏ ‏.‏\n"
